        "original_id": "6f443da0-d238-5266-be19-6a7642a3f925",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ali Eren Balıkel, Helen Mirren, Cem Adrian, Abdüllatif Şener, Suat Kılıç, Robert De Niro, Asuman Dabak\n- Places: Adana, Kilikya region, Turkey, Kuwait\n- Organizations: BAFTA Awards, Emmy Awards\n- Roles: Prime Minister of Kuwait, Sports and Youth Minister of Turkey\n- Projects: Kilikya’s Cafe Bar Restaurant, Prime Suspect, Jane Tennison\n\nFacts:\n- Helen Mirren was born on 26 July 1945 and is an English actor.\n- Helen Mirren won three consecutive BAFTA Awards for Best Actress from 1992 to 1994.\n- Helen Mirren won her first of several Emmy Awards in 1996 for playing police detective Jane Tennison in the British television series Prime Suspect.\n- Prime Suspect ran for seven seasons from 1991 to 2006.\n- Ali Eren Balıkel was born on 27 July 1979 in Adana and grew up in the ancient Kilikya region of Turkey.\n- Ali Eren Balıkel started Kilikya’s Cafe Bar Restaurant.\n- Kilikya’s Cafe Bar Restaurant hosted Cem Adrian, Abdüllatif Şener, Suat Kılıç, Helen Mirren, Robert De Niro, Asuman Dabak, and the Prime Minister of Kuwait.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
