        "text": "Page: Ali Eren Balıkel. Sentence: Ali Eren Balıkel was born on 27 July 1979, in Adana and grew up in the ancient Kilikya region of Turkey.\nPage: Ali Eren Balıkel. Sentence: He started a restaurant, Kilikya’s Cafe Bar Restaurant.\nPage: Ali Eren Balıkel. Sentence: Kilikya’s restaurant hosted a number of famous figures including singer Cem Adrian, politician Abdüllatif Şener, former Sports and Youth Minister of Turkey Suat Kılıç, Oscar award-winning actress Helen Mirren, American actor Robert De Niro and Turkish actress Asuman Dabak as well as the Prime Minister of Kuwait.\nPage: Helen Mirren. Sentence: Dame Helen Lydia Mirren, {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (\"née\" Mironoff; born 26 July 1945) is an English actor.\nPage: Helen Mirren. Sentence: Mirren won three consecutive BAFTA Awards for Best Actress between 1992 and 1994 and her first of several Emmy Awards in 1996 for her performance as police detective Jane Tennison on the British television series \"Prime Suspect\", which ran for seven seasons between 1991 and 2006.",
